* Noteworthy changes in release ?.? (????-??-??) [?]

** New features

  A full-screen interface with a menu bar (F9), a function-key bar,
  pages to switch between with 1-9, Alt-1..9 and Ctrl-PgUp/PgDn, and
  four color themes: classic, blue, dark and mono.

  The Overview page shows the host and system, uptime, load, and the
  use of the processors, memory and swap with their recent history.

  The CPU page shows how the processors' time is used, the use and
  frequency of each processor, the temperature, load, pressure and the
  rates of context switches, interrupts and new processes.

  The Memory page divides memory between programs, the kernel, buffers
  and cache, and shows swap, zram, paging rates, memory pressure and
  the processes with the most memory.

  The Disks page shows the throughput, busy time, latency and
  temperature of each disk, and the space on each local file system.

  The GPU page lists NVIDIA graphics processors with their
  temperature, utilization, video memory, power, clocks and fan speed,
  graphs of their history, and the processes using them.  Dials reads
  them through the NVIDIA driver's NVML library, loaded at run time,
  so it builds and runs on systems without it.

  The --demo option shows simulated data, and --once prints a
  plain-text report instead of starting the full-screen interface.
  The --sysroot option reads a saved copy of /proc and /sys, for
  testing.

